<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horio Yoshiharu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1542">1542</a>–<a href="/years/1611">1611</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Horio Yoshiharu was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and then sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> his family received Izumo and Oki, and he directed the building of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsue">Matsue</a> castle on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-shinji">Lake Shinji</a>, completed in 1611, the year he died. The Horio line died out in 1633.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horio-yoshiharu.jpg" alt="Horio Yoshiharu" width="320" height="703" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown (Inscription by Shunryō Gensai) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Horio_Yoshiharu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
